{"type":"tool_call","subtype":"completed","call_id":"tool_73cb23f4-7f06-454f-a72e-4ba166b233d","tool_call":{"webSearchToolCall":{"args":{"searchTerm":"IANA example domain","toolCallId":"tool_73cb23f4-7f06-454f-a72e-4ba166b233d"},"result":{"success":{"references":[{"title":"Web search results","url":"","chunk":"Links:\n1. [Example Domains](https://www.iana.org/help/example-domains)\n2. [IANA-managed Reserved Domains](https://www.iana.org/domains/reserved)\n3. [](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6761.html)\n4. [RFC 2606 - Reserved Top Level DNS Names](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2606)\n5. [](https://www.iana.org/assignments/special-use-domain-names/special-use-domain-names.txt)\n\nSynthesis:\nIANA reserves example.com, example.net, and example.org for documentation and illustrative examples. They may be used in documents without prior coordination, but cannot be registered or transferred. [1][2] RFC 6761 also reserves the broader example. domain and names beneath it for documentation use. [3]\n\nHighlights:\n<result id=\"1\">\n<title>Example Domains</title>\n<url>https://www.iana.org/help/example-domains</url>\n<content>Example Domains\n\n# Example Domains\n\nA number of domains such as `example.com` and `example.org` are maintained for documentation purposes. These domains may be used as illustrative examples in documents without prior coordination with us. They are not available for registration or transfer.\n\nWe provide a web service on the example domain hosts to provide basic information on the purpose of the domain. These web services are provided as best effort, but are not designed to support production applications. We strongly recommend you do not design applications that require the example domains to have operating HTTP service.\n\nDomain Names\n\n- Root Zone Registry\n- .INT Registry\n- .ARPA Registry\n- IDN Repository\n\nNumber Resources</content>\n</result>\n\n<result id=\"2\">\n<title>IANA-managed Reserved Domains</title>\n<url>https://www.iana.org/domains/reserved</url>\n<content>## Example domains\n\nAs described in RFC 2606 and RFC 6761, a number of domains such as example.com and example.org are maintained for documentation purposes. These domains may be used as illustrative examples in documents without prior coordination with us. They are not available for registration or transfer.</content>\n</result>\n\n<result id=\"3\">\n<title></title>\n<url>https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6761.html</url>\n<content>6.5.  Domain Name Reservation Considerations for Example Domains\n\n   The domains \"example.\", \"example.com.\", \"example.net.\",\n   \"example.org.\", and any names falling within those domains, are\n   special in the following ways:\n\n   1.  Users SHOULD understand that example names are reserved for use\n       in documentation.\n...\nresolution APIs\n...\nCaching DNS servers\n...\nexample names as\n...\n6.  DNS server operators SHOULD be aware that example names are\n       reserved for use in documentation.\n\n   7.  DNS Registries/Registrars MUST NOT grant requests to register\n       example names in the normal way to any person or entity.  All\n       example names are registered in perpetuity to IANA:\n...\nRFC 6761                Special-Use Domain Names           February 2013\n\n        Domain Name: EXAMPLE.COM\n        Registrar: RESERVED-INTERNET ASSIGNED NUMBERS AUTHORITY\n        Whois Server: whois.iana.org\n        Referral URL: http://res-dom.iana.org\n        Name Server: A.IANA-SERVERS.NET\n        Name Server: B.IANA-SERVERS.NET\n        Status: clientDeleteProhibited\n        Status: clientTransferProhibited\n        Status: clientUpdateProhibited\n        Updated Date: 26-mar-2004\n        Creation Date: 14-aug-1995\n        Expiration Date: 13-aug-2011\n\n   IANA currently maintains a web server providing a web page explaining\n   the purpose of example domains.\n...\nIANA has created a new registry of Special-Use Domain Names,\n   initially populated with the private-address reverse-mapping domains\n   and the Reserved Top Level DNS Names outlined above in Section 6.\n\n   When IANA ... request to record a new \"Special-Use Domain\n...\n\", it should verify, in consultation with the IESG,\n...\n226\n...\nIANA and the I\n...\nappropriate, I ... Name, and a</content>\n</result>\n\n<result id=\"4\">\n<title>RFC 2606 - Reserved Top Level DNS Names</title>\n<url>https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc2606</url>\n<content>3. Reserved Example Second Level Domain Names\n\n   The Internet Assigned Numbers Authority (IANA) also currently has the\n   following second level domain names reserved which can be used as\n   examples.\n...\n```\nRFC 2606              Reserved Top Level DNS Names             June 1999\n\n        example.com\n        example.net\n        example.org\n\n4. IANA Considerations\n\n   IANA has agreed to the four top level domain name reservations\n   specified in this document and will reserve them for the uses\n   indicated.</content>\n</result>\n\n<result id=\"5\">\n<title></title>\n<url>https://www.iana.org/assignments/special-use-domain-names/special-use-domain-names.txt</url>\n<content>Internet Assigned Numbers Authority\n • Domains\n • Protocols\n • Numbers\n • About\n\n Special-Use Domain Names\n\nCreated\n 2012-07-06\n\nLast Updated\n 2026-05-22\n\nAvailable Formats\n [IMG]\n XML [IMG]\n HTML [IMG]\n TXT\n\nRegistry Included Below\n\n • Special-Use Domain Names\n\nSpecial-Use Domain Names\n\nRegistration Procedure(s)\n\n Standards Action or IESG Approval\n\nReference\n [RFC 6761]\n\nNote\n\n The \"Special Use\" designation applies to both the listed domains and their subdomains.\n\nAvailable Formats\n [IMG]\n CSV\n\n Name Reference\nalt. [RFC 9476]\n6tisch.arpa. [RFC 9031]\neap.arpa. [RFC 9965]\neap-noob.arpa. (DEPRECATED) [RFC 9140]; [RFC 9965]\nhome.arpa. [RFC 8375]\n10.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n254.169.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6762]\n16.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n17.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n18.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n19.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n20.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n21.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n22.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n23.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n24.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n25.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n26.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n27.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n28.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n29.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n30.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n31.172.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n170.0.0.192.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 8880]\n171.0.0.192.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 8880]\n168.192.in-addr.arpa. [RFC 6761]\n8.e.f.ip6.arpa. [RFC 6762]\n9.e.f.ip6.arpa. [RFC 6762]\na.e.f.ip6.arpa. [RFC 6762]\nb.e.f.ip6.arpa. [RFC 6762]\nipv4only.arpa. [RFC 8880]\nresolver.arpa. [RFC 9462]\nservice.arpa. [RFC 9665]\nexample. [RFC 6761]\nexample.com. [RFC 6761]\nexample.net. [RFC 6761]\nexample.org. [RFC 6761]\ninvalid. [RFC 6761]\nlocal. [RFC 6762]\nlocalhost. [RFC 6761]\nonion. [RFC 7686]\ntest. [RFC 6761]\n\nLicensing Terms</content>\n</result>"},{"title":"","url":"https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6761.html","chunk":"Full page text written to file: /home/user/.cursor/projects/tmp-mge-workspaces-prj-demo/agent-tools/17177243-0923-4d38-aef6-3661c6c5e9fa.txt\nSize: 28.2 KB, 654 lines\nUse shell / grep / read_file on this path to inspect the page; no follow-up fetch is needed."}]}}},"hookAdditionalContexts":[],"toolCallId":"tool_73cb23f4-7f06-454f-a72e-4ba166b233d","startedAtMs":"1791946374158","completedAtMs":"1791946378037"},"model_call_id":"80cf642f-ba1c-45e7-90c5-123a76da7117-0-6xcs","session_id":"42457c32-d797-46ec-b399-acad3f0543ba","timestamp_ms":1791946378097}
